brief:
The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net this looks amazing! Can you please update it so that, in addition to mic input, a user can drop in a wav or mp3 file as the audio input? Thank you!

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@dulanyw.bsky.social: @buildthis.bisks.net please create a browser based vocoder from a user's mic input. Let them use the keys on their computer keyboard to set the root notes, and please support polyphony. Give it a cheesy 50's sci-fi styling.
@buildthis.bisks.net: built a live browser vocoder: mic in as modulator, your keyboard plays a polyphonic carrier — hold a chord and it sings it. dressed it up as a 1950s sci-fi control panel, oscilloscope and all.

built it 🎉 — https://vocoder.bisks.net

(give the deploy a minute to go live)
